WEBVTT

00:01.800 --> 00:04.957
Meet the AI Teaching Assistant, built for teaching

00:04.957 --> 00:07.545
and learning at Mae Fah Luang University.

00:08.445 --> 00:11.402
Three portals. One intelligent learning platform.

00:13.702 --> 00:17.647
Administrators manage accounts, courses, and platform policies.

00:18.247 --> 00:22.738
Teachers publish course content and configure the AI tools for each course.

00:23.338 --> 00:26.821
Students follow their courses and study with an AI assistant

00:26.821 --> 00:29.201
that answers from their course materials.

00:32.851 --> 00:36.277
Administrators sign in through a dedicated console,

00:36.277 --> 00:39.569
restricted to university IT and authorized staff.

00:40.780 --> 00:44.652
The console opens on course management. Every course is listed

00:44.652 --> 00:48.087
with its status, and search narrows the list instantly.

00:48.987 --> 00:51.264
Each course shows its teacher, students,

00:51.264 --> 00:55.307
documents, and class sections, including which teachers may post to it.

00:56.207 --> 00:59.052
The organization overview summarizes users,

00:59.052 --> 01:03.221
courses, enrollments, and indexed course documents at a glance.

01:04.121 --> 01:07.177
Under Members, administrators manage student,

01:07.177 --> 01:11.524
teacher, and administrator accounts, with CSV import and export.

01:12.424 --> 01:15.105
System policies control Google sign-in,

01:15.105 --> 01:19.092
LINE notifications, and strict course-grounded AI answers.

01:19.992 --> 01:25.787
Consent records and a complete audit log support PDPA and GDPR compliance.

01:29.177 --> 01:31.321
Teachers sign in to the Teacher Portal,

01:31.321 --> 01:33.904
where My Courses lists every course they teach.

01:39.606 --> 01:44.807
Dr. Anan Suwan opens Seminar in Software Engineering and starts a new announcement.

01:45.707 --> 01:50.104
The teacher writes the announcement and attaches the week's materials:

01:50.104 --> 01:54.312
a PDF reading guide, a Word review template, and PowerPoint slides.

01:56.921 --> 02:01.386
Once posted, the announcement appears in the course feed with every file linked.

02:02.286 --> 02:06.106
The same files are added to the Materials tab automatically,

02:06.106 --> 02:08.843
listed by file name, with no second upload.

02:09.743 --> 02:13.634
The AI Assistant tab brings together the course's AI tools:

02:13.634 --> 02:17.525
chat, assignments, flashcards, quizzes, FAQs, and settings.

02:18.425 --> 02:23.686
Teachers add course FAQs, which the chatbot prioritizes when it answers students.

02:24.586 --> 02:29.808
Quizzes are generated by AI from a course material. Five multiple-choice questions

02:29.808 --> 02:34.967
are written from the seminar guide, and the quiz goes live for enrolled students.

02:35.867 --> 02:39.527
In settings, teachers choose the chatbot's tone and model.

02:39.527 --> 02:44.449
The default model runs locally, so course content stays on the campus network.

02:45.349 --> 02:48.559
Analytics shows question trends, activity by course,

02:48.559 --> 02:51.151
and the questions students ask most often.

02:52.051 --> 02:57.234
A calendar timeline and the MFU Campus Guide complete the teacher's workspace.

03:00.951 --> 03:05.200
Students sign in to the Student Portal and see all of their enrolled courses.

03:11.165 --> 03:15.674
The notification bell already lists the new announcement and each attached file.

03:16.574 --> 03:20.286
Inside the course, the teacher's announcement appears with its files.

03:21.186 --> 03:24.493
The Materials tab holds the same files, ready to open.

03:25.393 --> 03:29.510
Opening the reading guide displays the PDF right in the browser.

03:30.410 --> 03:35.312
In the AI Assistant, the student asks how many papers the literature review needs.

03:37.482 --> 03:42.504
The answer comes from the course materials: twelve to fifteen papers,

03:42.504 --> 03:47.163
plus a reproduction plan, as stated in the CSD323 Seminar Guide.

03:48.063 --> 03:50.845
Study tools also include flashcards, quizzes,

03:50.845 --> 03:55.236
and a planner, and the quiz the teacher just generated is already here.

03:56.136 --> 03:57.994
Assignments list each deadline,

03:57.994 --> 04:01.230
and a reminder is created automatically one day ahead.

04:02.130 --> 04:06.896
The calendar brings classes, tasks, and course updates together in one timeline.

04:08.808 --> 04:12.116
Together, the three portals form one connected workflow.

04:12.116 --> 04:15.718
The administrator sets up the course and assigns its teacher.

04:16.318 --> 04:19.625
The teacher publishes an announcement with the week's materials.

04:20.225 --> 04:24.828
Those files reach every enrolled student, in the announcement and in Materials.

04:25.428 --> 04:29.616
And students get answers drawn from the same course content, at any hour.

04:31.616 --> 04:35.146
Course-grounded AI support, materials shared once,

04:35.146 --> 04:39.098
local AI by default, and role-based access for everyone.

04:39.698 --> 04:43.873
AI Teaching Assistant. Empowering teaching. Enhancing learning.
